          <h2>2. Friendship Across Cultures: Similar Goals, Different Paths</h2>

          <p>
            Despite our differences, friendship has universal ingredients: trust, kindness,
            humor, and shared experiences. But how those values are expressed varies by culture.
            Understanding these differences helps you adapt and avoid miscommunication.
          </p>

          <h3>Individualist vs. Collectivist Perspectives</h3>

          <p>
            Researchers sometimes use concepts such as <strong>individualism</strong> and
            <strong>collectivism</strong> to study how societies may differ in the relative
            importance they place on individual goals, group relationships, and social obligations.
            These concepts can help explain broad patterns, but they do not predict how a
            particular person will behave.
          </p>

          <div
            class="table-scroll"
            style="width:100%;max-width:100%;overflow-x:auto;-webkit-overflow-scrolling:touch;margin:24px 0;"
          >
            <table
